#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:40002
msgid "Voronoi Cells and the Area Distribution of Sample Points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:40005
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"By constructing the Voronoi tessellation on the sphere, shown as the "
"green grid in the figure above, we can compute the area associated with "
"each sample point. For an ideal uniform sampling, the Voronoi area of "
"each point should be close to $\\frac{4\\pi}{N}$. The figure below shows "
"the distribution of Voronoi-cell areas for the case $N=256$:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:40007
msgid "**Area distribution**: most regions have areas close to the ideal value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:40008
msgid "**Error range**: for most sample points, the error is within 2%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:50002
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Using the spherical Voronoi tessellation, shown as the green grid in the "
"figure above, we can compute the area associated with each sample point. "
"For ideal uniform sampling, the Voronoi area of every sample point should"
" be equal to $\\frac{4\\pi}{N}$. The figure below shows the distribution "
"of Voronoi-cell areas for all sample points. Most regions are close to "
"the ideal value, and for most sample points the error is within 2%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:70002
msgid "Definition and Analysis of Sampling Uniformity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:70005
msgid "We define the uniformity of the sampling as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:70007
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{Uniformity} = 1 - \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\left|A_i - "
"\\frac{4\\pi}{N}\\right|}{4\\pi},\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/details/spherical_sampling.ipynb:70011
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where $A_i$ is the Voronoi-cell area of the $i$-th sample point. If "
"$\\text{Uniformity} \\approx 1$, the sampling is considered highly "
"uniform."
msgstr ""

